    description: "WI-mafik Level 1b child (multi-gap). The Rust analyzer fails three import-times-call shapes: (1) `use std::fs::write` + bare `write(...)` emits no calls edge at all; (2) aliased name (`use std::fs::create_dir as mkdir` + `mkdir(...)`) preserves the alias rather than resolving to `create_dir`; (3) qualified call after `use std::fs;` (`fs::read_to_string(...)`) emits dst missing the `std::` prefix (analyzer doesn't connect `fs` back to `std::fs`). Repro in polyglot fixture::rust. All three are Rust analogs of the WI-zigah dotted-submodule resolution that landed for Python. Fix lives in packages/hypergumbo-lang-mainstream/src/hypergumbo_lang_mainstream/rust.py (may also touch rust_def_use.py) — call-site resolution against `use` declarations. Acceptance: remove xfail_reason for rust in the polyglot fixture without other test changes."  # d956
    fields: {}  # d956
